 "tagline": "Trained on 36 automatic variants of one clip, the tracker completes 100% of 7 variants it never saw, with 0% falls. The best single-clip policy manages 66% and falls 34% of the time.",
 "story": {
  "shown": "The front kick phone video, retargeted to the G1, then turned into variants with nothing action-specific: mirrored, faster and slower, bigger and smaller, unevenly re-timed. Each variant gets its own key-moment spec from the same compiler.",
  "learned": "Two policies trained on all the training variants at once, warm-started from the clip's tracking policy. Each environment plays one variant and is scored against that variant's spec.",
  "how": "7 held-out variants outside the training range (mirrored, 0.6x tempo, 0.8x size; mirrored, 1.6x tempo, 1.2x size; 0.5x tempo; 0.7x size; 1.25x size; uneven tempo 0.5; 2x tempo), 64 rollouts each. Success: every key moment in order, no fall."
 },
